      "type": "frame",
      "id": "R9Fmr",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 150,
      "name": "BRIEF — Capture · mobile",
      "clip": true,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 1060,
      "fill": "$paper",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-2xl",
      "stroke": "$line",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 10,
      "padding": 32,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "rT0br",
          "name": "Heading",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "BRIEF — Capture · mobile",
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 14,
          "fontWeight": "700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "V2fSju",
          "name": "Body",
          "fill": "$graphite",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 0.3.0 · brief-schema: 1 · updated: 2026-09-30\n1. PURPOSE\nThe desktop flow (see the desktop brief) adapted to a phone: pick a ready-made base and adjust it at once without an expert, or describe a piece with an optional expert the person connects with their own key. The bases never need the expert.\n2. ENTRY POINTS\nOpening the app with no design.\n3. SCREENS (columns are the steps; every screen here is a proposal)\n- Step 1 · Home: Catalog first, without and with an expert. The header is compact (the mark, a status dot with a short label, \"Sin experto\" or \"Con experto\", and Ajustes as an icon). The door \"Diseña el tuyo\" is a compact row under the headline (Adrian's choice): its button is secondary \"Conectar experto\" without an expert and primary \"Nuevo diseño\" with one. The bases come right after in two columns, the category chips scroll sideways, and the last tile, full width, is \"¿No está el tuyo?\".\n- Step 2 · Adjust your base: the base's 3D on top (the Studio's mobile pattern) and the questions below: the space in cm, what the ficha lets change (counters, for this sideboard drawers, doors and open niches) and the finish; the sheets and the approximate cost and \"Abrir en el Studio\" and \"Saltar y usar la base tal cual\" stay fixed at the bottom (Adrian's choice).\n- Step 3 · Connect the expert: a full-screen sheet instead of a floating dialog, because of the keyboard; new connection (the passphrase is optional) and the saved-key state; the actions are fixed at the bottom.\n- Step 4 · Describe your furniture: without an expert (banner and \"Conectar experto\"), empty and with photos. The description stays first, as on desktop (Adrian's choice), then the space in cm (three fields) and the photos last, two per row (Adrian's note); the no-expert alert is a rounded card with a badge so it is not lost; the main button and the way back to the bases are fixed at the bottom of the screen.\n- Step 5 · Analyzing: the sketch, the clock under it, the stages and a footer history of the last three real steps.\n- \"To review\" column: photo reading failed and design failed, still the old shell (the simulated expert cannot produce them). \"States to redraw in the new shell\": choosing a photo's view, writing a photo note, five photos and kind changed, still the old shell.\n4. BUSINESS RULES\nSame as desktop: the main button of the custom path is disabled until there are 15 characters or a photo; the space is asked in cm and the code takes mm today; each photo is read when added.\n5. COPY SOURCE\nSame as desktop. NEW on the phone: \"Sin experto\" and \"Con experto\" (the short status), \"Con fotos o una descripción.\" (the door), the 2-column grid's notes.\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\nThe keyboard over the sheets, the horizontal scroll of the chips and the motion (the fade of the history). The states above waiting in the side columns.\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nUI-29, UI-30, UI-31, UI-32, UI-35\n8. HISTORY\n→ LOG frame.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-mono",
          "fontSize": 12,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
